# 2. FRONTEND ENGINEERING PRINCIPLES

ZyrionOS frontend must follow these principles.

## 2.1 Production First

Every implementation must be designed for real production use.

The frontend must not depend on:

- Demo-only architecture
- Temporary UI hacks
- Fake API responses
- Fake deployment URLs
- Unnecessary mock data
- Duplicated components
- Duplicated API clients
- Hardcoded business logic
- Placeholder production behavior

Temporary development tools may exist during development,
but they must not become part of the production architecture.

---

## 2.2 Reusable First

Before creating a new component, determine whether an existing
component can be reused.

Shared components should be used wherever the same interaction
or visual pattern appears.

Examples:

- Button
- Input
- Textarea
- Select
- Modal
- Drawer
- Card
- Badge
- Table
- Tabs
- Dropdown
- Tooltip
- Toast
- Loading State
- Empty State
- Error State

A page must not create a private version of a global component
without a documented reason.

---

## 2.3 Single Responsibility

Each component must have one primary responsibility.

Avoid giant components that control unrelated systems.

BAD:

Dashboard.jsx
- Navigation
- Authentication
- API requests
- Billing
- Project logic
- Tables
- Modals
- Notifications
- Settings

PREFERRED:

Dashboard
├── DashboardHeader
├── DashboardOverview
├── ProjectSummary
├── UsageSummary
├── ActivityFeed
└── DashboardActions

---

## 2.4 Predictability

A developer should be able to understand where a feature belongs
without searching through unrelated files.

The same architectural pattern must be used throughout the product.

---

## 2.5 Consistency

Equivalent actions must behave equivalently across the application.

Examples:

- Save buttons behave consistently.
- Delete confirmations behave consistently.
- Loading states behave consistently.
- Error messages behave consistently.
- Notifications behave consistently.
- Navigation behaves consistently.

